// PORT AZUL: the procedural coastal city.
//
// A seeded grid of streets with a tower-filled downtown, a neon strip, houses,
// shops, civic buildings, a container port, a highway bridge, a boardwalk with
// a Ferris wheel, a fishing pier, a lighthouse, a beach and the open sea. Every
// mesh is built from primitives and canvas textures — there are no assets.
//
// World axes, in metres: +x is east, +z is south. Streets sit on a PITCH grid
// centred on the origin; the shoreline is well south of the last street. The
// class below owns the static geometry plus the few things that animate (the
// wheel, the traffic lights, the palms, the surf, the day/night pass), and it
// answers the queries the rest of the game asks of the world: collision
// footprints, walkable ground height, water tests, spawn points and the HUD's
// street / district names.
